/-!
# C.Schema: the generated tree-sitter-C schema

Generated by `tools/SchemaMain.wiz` from `grammars/tree-sitter-c/node-types.json`
(a real excerpt of tree-sitter-c, 132 named entries). **Do not edit**: rerun
`grail run scry-schema -- grammars/tree-sitter-c/node-types.json`, or
`grail build schema`. `tests/codegen.wiz` fails when this file is stale.

`C.Kind` has one constructor per concrete named node kind; `C.Kind.sym` is the
generated ordinal (`U16`) and `C.Kind.idx` the same in `U32`, so a kind can index
the native store's column. The tree-sitter shim checks `sym` against
`ts_language_symbol_name` when it lands. `C.fields` gives each field's
cardinality and allowed **concrete** kinds (supertypes expanded); `C.allows` is
the runtime check. Typed ids (`C.NodeId k`, `C.FieldId f`, `C.Edge`) carry the
kind/field in the type only (phantom, 22e). Every tree may contain ERROR/MISSING
nodes, so accessors over a store are `Option` (design §4.2).
-/

